IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa8-helpers`

-- coa8-part15-small.l4: Companies Act 2006, Part 15 (accounts and reports), Chapter 1 (introduction), ss 380 to 385:
-- the scheme of the Part, the small companies regime, micro-entities, and quoted and unquoted companies
-- (lines 4845-4949 of ukpga-2006-46.txt). LAYER 1: the law, objectively.
-- The thresholds are those the text states (section 382(3), 383(4), 384A(4)); a substitution by regulations would change the answers.
-- Money is in pounds; a proportion of a year is a NUMBER fraction (1 is a whole year).

§ `Part 15: Accounts and reports`

§§ `Chapter 1: Introduction`

-- s 380(2) ("In certain respects different provisions apply to different kinds of company") creates no rule: inert, reason 1.
-- s 380(3) and (4) are blank in this text ("..."): repealed or blank.

-- src:4849 | (1) The requirements of this Part as to accounts and reports apply in relation to each financial year of a company.
@ref s 380(1) Scheme of this Part (src:4849)
GIVEN `the period is a financial year of a company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 380(1) the requirements of this Part as to accounts and reports apply in relation to the period` MEANS
    IF `the period is a financial year of a company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "apply in relation to each financial year of a company"

-- ---- s 381: companies subject to the small companies regime --------------------------------------------------

-- src:4855 | The small companies regime . . . applies to a company for a financial year in relation to which the company—
-- src:4856 | (a) qualifies as small (see sections 382 and 383), and
-- src:4857 | (b) is not excluded from the regime (see section 384).
@ref s 381 Companies subject to the small companies regime (src:4855-4857)
GIVEN `s 382 the company qualifies as small` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 384 the company is excluded from the small companies regime` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 381 the small companies regime applies to the company for the financial year` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "applies to a company for a financial year in relation to which the company— (a) qualifies as small (see sections 382 and 383), and (b) is not excluded from the regime"
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) where a seam answer from sections 382 to 384 is NOTHING
    `s 362 helper both answers` `s 382 the company qualifies as small` (`s 362 helper the opposite answer` `s 384 the company is excluded from the small companies regime`)

-- ---- s 382: companies qualifying as small: general -------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4863 | 1. Turnover | Not more than £15 million
@ref s 382(3) The qualifying conditions: turnover (row 1) (src:4863)
`s 382(3) the turnover limit, in pounds` MEANS 15000000

-- src:4864 | 2. Balance sheet total | Not more than £7.5 million
@ref s 382(3) The qualifying conditions: balance sheet total (row 2) (src:4864)
`s 382(3) the balance sheet total limit, in pounds` MEANS 7500000

-- src:4865 | 3. Number of employees | Not more than 50
@ref s 382(3) The qualifying conditions: number of employees (row 3) (src:4865)
`s 382(3) the employees limit` MEANS 50

-- src:4866 | (4) For a period that is a company's financial year but not in fact a year the maximum figures for turnover must be proportionately adjusted.
@ref s 382(4) Proportionate adjustment of the turnover figure for a period that is not a year (src:4866)
GIVEN `the maximum figure for turnover` IS A NUMBER
      `the length of the period as a proportion of a year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 382(4) the maximum figure for turnover adjusted to the length of the period` MEANS
    `the maximum figure for turnover` TIMES `the length of the period as a proportion of a year`

-- src:4867 | (5) The balance sheet total means the aggregate of the amounts shown as assets in the company's balance sheet.
@ref s 382(5) The balance sheet total (src:4867)
GIVEN `the amounts shown as assets in the company's balance sheet` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 382(5) the balance sheet total` MEANS
    sum `the amounts shown as assets in the company's balance sheet`

-- src:4868 | (6) The number of employees means the average number of persons employed by the company in the year, determined as follows—
-- src:4869 | (a) find for each month in the financial year the number of persons employed under contracts of service by the company in that month (whether throughout the month or not),
-- src:4870 | (b) add together the monthly totals, and
-- src:4871 | (c) divide by the number of months in the financial year.
@ref s 382(6) The number of employees (src:4868-4871)
-- One entry per month of the financial year: the number of persons employed under contracts of service in that month (whether
-- throughout the month or not). The divisor is the number of months in the financial year, that is, the number of entries.
GIVEN `the number of persons employed under contracts of service by the company in each month of the financial year` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 382(6) the number of employees` MEANS
    IF null `the number of persons employed under contracts of service by the company in each month of the financial year`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a financial year with no months has no average
    ELSE JUST (sum `the number of persons employed under contracts of service by the company in each month of the financial year` DIVIDED BY count `the number of persons employed under contracts of service by the company in each month of the financial year`)

-- src:4863 | 1. Turnover | Not more than £15 million
@ref s 382(3) Row 1: turnover (src:4863)
GIVEN turnover IS A NUMBER
      `the length of the financial year as a proportion of a year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 382(3) row 1 the turnover is not more than the limit` MEANS
    IF turnover AT MOST `s 382(4) the maximum figure for turnover adjusted to the length of the period` `s 382(3) the turnover limit, in pounds` `the length of the financial year as a proportion of a year`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "1. Turnover | Not more than £15 million"

-- src:4864 | 2. Balance sheet total | Not more than £7.5 million
@ref s 382(3) Row 2: balance sheet total (src:4864)
GIVEN `balance sheet total` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 382(3) row 2 the balance sheet total is not more than the limit` MEANS
    IF `balance sheet total` AT MOST `s 382(3) the balance sheet total limit, in pounds`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "2. Balance sheet total | Not more than £7.5 million"

-- src:4865 | 3. Number of employees | Not more than 50
@ref s 382(3) Row 3: number of employees (src:4865)
GIVEN `number of employees` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 382(3) row 3 the number of employees is not more than the limit` MEANS
    IF `number of employees` AT MOST `s 382(3) the employees limit`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "3. Number of employees | Not more than 50"

-- src:4862 | (3) The qualifying conditions are met by a company in a year in which it satisfies two or more of the following requirements—
-- src:4863 | 1. Turnover | Not more than £15 million
-- src:4864 | 2. Balance sheet total | Not more than £7.5 million
-- src:4865 | 3. Number of employees | Not more than 50
@ref s 382(3) The qualifying conditions: two or more of the three requirements (src:4862-4865)
GIVEN turnover IS A NUMBER
      `balance sheet total` IS A NUMBER
      `number of employees` IS A NUMBER
      `the length of the financial year as a proportion of a year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 382(3) the qualifying conditions are met in the year` MEANS
    IF count (filter (GIVEN r YIELD r EQUALS JUST TRUE)
                 (LIST `s 382(3) row 1 the turnover is not more than the limit` turnover `the length of the financial year as a proportion of a year`,
                       `s 382(3) row 2 the balance sheet total is not more than the limit` `balance sheet total`,
                       `s 382(3) row 3 the number of employees is not more than the limit` `number of employees`)) AT LEAST 2
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The qualifying conditions are met by a company in a year in which it satisfies two or more of the following requirements"

-- src:4859 | (1) A company qualifies as small in relation to its first financial year if the qualifying conditions are met in that year.
@ref s 382(1) Qualifying as small in the first financial year (src:4859)
GIVEN `the qualifying conditions are met in that year` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 382(1) the company qualifies as small in its first financial year` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the qualifying conditions are met in that year`
    WHEN JUST met THEN
        IF met
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company qualifies as small in relation to its first financial year if the qualifying conditions are met in that year"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the qualifying conditions are not known

-- (2): a change (the company meets, or ceases to meet, the conditions) affects its qualification only if it occurs in two
-- consecutive financial years. "Meets or ceases to meet" is read against the status the company had in the previous year.
-- src:4861 | (2) In relation to a subsequent financial year, where on its balance sheet date a company meets or ceases to meet the qualifying conditions, that affects its qualification as a small company only if it occurs in two consecutive financial years.
@ref s 382(2) A change affects qualification only if it occurs in two consecutive financial years (src:4861)
GIVEN `the qualifying conditions are met in this year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the qualifying conditions were met in the previous year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company qualified as small in the previous year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 382(2) the change in whether the qualifying conditions are met affects the company's qualification` MEANS
    IF `the qualifying conditions are met in this year` EQUALS `the company qualified as small in the previous year`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where on its balance sheet date a company meets or ceases to meet the qualifying conditions": there is no change this year
    ELSE IF `the qualifying conditions are met in this year` EQUALS `the qualifying conditions were met in the previous year`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that affects its qualification as a small company only if it occurs in two consecutive financial years"

-- src:4860 | (1A) Subject to subsection (2), a company qualifies as small in relation to a subsequent financial year if the qualifying conditions are met in that year.
@ref s 382(1A) Qualifying as small in a subsequent financial year (src:4860)
GIVEN `the qualifying conditions are met in this year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the qualifying conditions were met in the previous year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company qualified as small in the previous year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 382(1A) the company qualifies as small in a subsequent financial year` MEANS
    IF `the qualifying conditions are met in this year` EQUALS `the company qualified as small in the previous year`
    THEN JUST `the qualifying conditions are met in this year` -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words) where not met: "if the qualifying conditions are met in that year"
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 382(2) the change in whether the qualifying conditions are met affects the company's qualification` `the qualifying conditions are met in this year` `the qualifying conditions were met in the previous year` `the company qualified as small in the previous year`
         WHEN JUST affects THEN
             IF affects
             THEN JUST `the qualifying conditions are met in this year`
             ELSE JUST `the company qualified as small in the previous year` -- the change does not yet affect qualification (subsection (2))
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

