    IF `the qualifying conditions are met by the group in this year` EQUALS `the group qualified as small in the previous year`
    THEN JUST `the qualifying conditions are met by the group in this year` -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words) where not met: "if the qualifying conditions are met in that year"
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 383(3) the change in whether the group meets the qualifying conditions affects the group's qualification` `the qualifying conditions are met by the group in this year` `the qualifying conditions were met by the group in the previous year` `the group qualified as small in the previous year`
         WHEN JUST affects THEN
