GIVEN `s 384(2) it qualified as small in relation to its last financial year ending on or before the end of the financial year to which the accounts relate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 384(3) the company is a small company for the purposes of subsection (2)` MEANS
    IF `s 384(2) it qualified as small in relation to its last financial year ending on or before the end of the financial year to which the accounts relate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company is a small company for the purposes of subsection (2) if it qualified as small"

-- One member of a group, with the facts each limb of subsection (2) asks. Borrowed terms (Part 4A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000,
-- e-money issuer, MiFID investment firm, UCITS management company, insurance market activity, Master Trust scheme) are MAYBE BOOLEAN inputs.
-- src:4901 | (2) A group is ineligible if any of its members is—
-- src:4902 | (a) a traded company,
-- src:4903 | (b) a body corporate (other than a company) whose shares are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market,
-- src:4904 | (c) a person (other than a small company) who has permission under Part 4A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (c. 8) to carry on a regulated activity,
-- src:4905 | (ca) an e-money issuer,
-- src:4906 | (d) a small company that is an authorised insurance company, a banking company, ... a MiFID investment firm or a UCITS management company, or
-- src:4907 | (e) a person who carries on insurance market activity or
-- src:4908 | (f) a scheme funder of a Master Trust scheme within the meanings given by section 39(1) of the Pension Schemes Act 2017 or section 39(1) of the Pension Schemes Act (Northern Ireland) 2021 (interpretation of Part 1).
@ref s 384(2) A group is ineligible if any of its members is of a named kind (src:4901-4908)
DECLARE `s 384(2) member of the group` HAS
    `s 384(2) a traded company (section 360C)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 384(2) a body corporate other than a company whose shares are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 384(2) a person with permission under Part 4A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 to carry on a regulated activity` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 384(2) an e-money issuer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 384(2) an authorised insurance company, a banking company, a MiFID investment firm or a UCITS management company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 384(2) a person who carries on insurance market activity` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 384(2) a scheme funder of a Master Trust scheme within the meanings given by section 39(1) of the Pension Schemes Act 2017 or the Pension Schemes Act (Northern Ireland) 2021` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 384(2) it qualified as small in relation to its last financial year ending on or before the end of the financial year to which the accounts relate` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:4901 | (2) A group is ineligible if any of its members is—
-- src:4902 | (a) a traded company,
-- src:4903 | (b) a body corporate (other than a company) whose shares are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market,
-- src:4904 | (c) a person (other than a small company) who has permission under Part 4A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (c. 8) to carry on a regulated activity,
-- src:4905 | (ca) an e-money issuer,
-- src:4906 | (d) a small company that is an authorised insurance company, a banking company, ... a MiFID investment firm or a UCITS management company, or
-- src:4907 | (e) a person who carries on insurance market activity or
-- src:4908 | (f) a scheme funder of a Master Trust scheme within the meanings given by section 39(1) of the Pension Schemes Act 2017 or section 39(1) of the Pension Schemes Act (Northern Ireland) 2021 (interpretation of Part 1).
@ref s 384(2) A group is ineligible if any of its members is of a named kind (src:4901-4908)
GIVEN member IS A `s 384(2) member of the group`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 384(2) the member is of a kind that makes the group ineligible` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A group is ineligible if any of its members is"
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) where a borrowed answer is not known and no other limb decides
    `s 362 helper some answer`
        (LIST (member's `s 384(2) a traded company (section 360C)`),
              JUST (member's `s 384(2) a body corporate other than a company whose shares are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market`),
              `s 362 helper both answers` (member's `s 384(2) a person with permission under Part 4A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 to carry on a regulated activity`) (`s 362 helper the opposite answer` small),
              member's `s 384(2) an e-money issuer`,
              `s 362 helper both answers` small (member's `s 384(2) an authorised insurance company, a banking company, a MiFID investment firm or a UCITS management company`),
              member's `s 384(2) a person who carries on insurance market activity`,
              member's `s 384(2) a scheme funder of a Master Trust scheme within the meanings given by section 39(1) of the Pension Schemes Act 2017 or the Pension Schemes Act (Northern Ireland) 2021`)
    WHERE
        -- (c) is "a person (other than a small company)" with permission under Part 4A; (d) is "a small company that is" an insurer, bank, MiFID firm or UCITS manager
        small MEANS `s 384(3) the company is a small company for the purposes of subsection (2)` (member's `s 384(2) it qualified as small in relation to its last financial year ending on or before the end of the financial year to which the accounts relate`)

-- src:4901 | (2) A group is ineligible if any of its members is—
-- src:4902 | (a) a traded company,
-- src:4903 | (b) a body corporate (other than a company) whose shares are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market,
-- src:4904 | (c) a person (other than a small company) who has permission under Part 4A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (c. 8) to carry on a regulated activity,
-- src:4905 | (ca) an e-money issuer,
-- src:4906 | (d) a small company that is an authorised insurance company, a banking company, ... a MiFID investment firm or a UCITS management company, or
-- src:4907 | (e) a person who carries on insurance market activity or
-- src:4908 | (f) a scheme funder of a Master Trust scheme within the meanings given by section 39(1) of the Pension Schemes Act 2017 or section 39(1) of the Pension Schemes Act (Northern Ireland) 2021 (interpretation of Part 1).
@ref s 384(2) A group is ineligible if any of its members is of a named kind (src:4901-4908)
GIVEN members IS A LIST OF `s 384(2) member of the group`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 384(2) the group is ineligible` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A group is ineligible if any of its members is" (no member is of a named kind)
    `s 362 helper some answer` (map (GIVEN m YIELD `s 384(2) the member is of a kind that makes the group ineligible` m) members)

-- src:4894 | (1) The small companies regime does not apply to a company that ... was at any time within the financial year to which the accounts relate—
-- src:4895 | (a) a public company,
-- src:4896 | (b) a company that—
-- src:4897 | (i) is an authorised insurance company, a banking company, an e-money issuer, a MiFID investment firm or a UCITS management company, or
-- src:4898 | (ii) carries on insurance market activity, or
-- src:4899 | (iii) is a scheme funder of a Master Trust scheme within the meanings given by section 39(1) of the Pension Schemes Act 2017 or section 39(1) of the Pension Schemes Act (Northern Ireland) 2021 (interpretation of Part 1), or
-- src:4900 | (c) a member of an ineligible group.
@ref s 384(1) Companies excluded from the small companies regime (src:4894-4900)
GIVEN `s 4(2) the company was at any time within the financial year a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1165(2) the company was at any time within the financial year an authorised insurance company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1164(2) the company was at any time within the financial year a banking company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company was at any time within the financial year an e-money issuer, a MiFID investment firm or a UCITS management company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company at any time within the financial year carried on insurance market activity` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company was at any time within the financial year a scheme funder of a Master Trust scheme` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 384(2) the company was at any time within the financial year a member of an ineligible group` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 384(1) the company is excluded from the small companies regime` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The small companies regime does not apply to a company that ... was at any time within the financial year to which the accounts relate" (read with section 381(b), "is not excluded from the regime (see section 384)": fork F5)
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) where a borrowed answer is not known and no other limb decides
    `s 362 helper some answer`
        (LIST JUST `s 4(2) the company was at any time within the financial year a public company`,
              JUST `s 1165(2) the company was at any time within the financial year an authorised insurance company`,
              JUST `s 1164(2) the company was at any time within the financial year a banking company`,
              `the company was at any time within the financial year an e-money issuer, a MiFID investment firm or a UCITS management company`,
              `the company at any time within the financial year carried on insurance market activity`,
              `the company was at any time within the financial year a scheme funder of a Master Trust scheme`,
              `s 384(2) the company was at any time within the financial year a member of an ineligible group`)

-- ---- s 384A: companies qualifying as micro-entities --------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Subsections (1), (2), (3), (5), (6) and (7) repeat the words of section 382(1), (1A), (2), (4), (5) and (6) with "micro-entity" for "small";
-- the same rules are called, with the micro-entity thresholds of subsection (4).

-- src:4915 | 1. Turnover | Not more than £1 million
@ref s 384A(4) The micro-entity qualifying conditions: turnover (row 1) (src:4915)
`s 384A(4) the turnover limit, in pounds` MEANS 1000000

-- src:4916 | 2. Balance sheet total | Not more than £500,000
@ref s 384A(4) The micro-entity qualifying conditions: balance sheet total (row 2) (src:4916)
`s 384A(4) the balance sheet total limit, in pounds` MEANS 500000

-- src:4917 | 3. Number of employees | Not more than 10
@ref s 384A(4) The micro-entity qualifying conditions: number of employees (row 3) (src:4917)
`s 384A(4) the employees limit` MEANS 10

-- src:4918 | (5) For a period that is a company’s financial year but not in fact a year the maximum figures for turnover must be proportionately adjusted.
@ref s 384A(5) Proportionate adjustment of the turnover figure for a period that is not a year (src:4918)
GIVEN `the length of the financial year as a proportion of a year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 384A(5) the maximum figure for turnover adjusted to the length of the period` MEANS
    `s 382(4) the maximum figure for turnover adjusted to the length of the period` `s 384A(4) the turnover limit, in pounds` `the length of the financial year as a proportion of a year`

-- src:4919 | (6) The balance sheet total means the aggregate of the amounts shown as assets in the company’s balance sheet.
@ref s 384A(6) The balance sheet total (src:4919)
GIVEN `the amounts shown as assets in the company's balance sheet` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 384A(6) the balance sheet total` MEANS
    `s 382(5) the balance sheet total` `the amounts shown as assets in the company's balance sheet`

-- src:4920 | (7) The number of employees means the average number of persons employed by the company in the year, determined as follows—
-- src:4921 | (a) find for each month in the financial year the number of persons employed under contracts of service by the company in that month (whether throughout the month or not),
-- src:4922 | (b) add together the monthly totals, and
-- src:4923 | (c) divide by the number of months in the financial year.
@ref s 384A(7) The number of employees (src:4920-4923)
GIVEN `the number of persons employed under contracts of service by the company in each month of the financial year` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 384A(7) the number of employees` MEANS
    `s 382(6) the number of employees` `the number of persons employed under contracts of service by the company in each month of the financial year`

-- src:4914 | (4) The qualifying conditions are met by a company in a year in which it satisfies two or more of the following requirements—
-- src:4915 | 1. Turnover | Not more than £1 million
-- src:4916 | 2. Balance sheet total | Not more than £500,000
-- src:4917 | 3. Number of employees | Not more than 10
@ref s 384A(4) The micro-entity qualifying conditions: two or more of the three requirements (src:4914-4917)
GIVEN turnover IS A NUMBER
      `balance sheet total` IS A NUMBER
      `number of employees` IS A NUMBER
      `the length of the financial year as a proportion of a year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 384A(4) the qualifying conditions are met in the year` MEANS
    IF count (filter (GIVEN r YIELD r)
                 (LIST turnover AT MOST `s 384A(5) the maximum figure for turnover adjusted to the length of the period` `the length of the financial year as a proportion of a year`,
                       `balance sheet total` AT MOST `s 384A(4) the balance sheet total limit, in pounds`,
                       `number of employees` AT MOST `s 384A(4) the employees limit`)) AT LEAST 2
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The qualifying conditions are met by a company in a year in which it satisfies two or more of the following requirements"

-- src:4911 | (1) A company qualifies as a micro-entity in relation to its first financial year if the qualifying conditions are met in that year.
@ref s 384A(1) Qualifying as a micro-entity in the first financial year (src:4911)
GIVEN `the qualifying conditions are met in that year` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 384A(1) the company qualifies as a micro-entity in its first financial year` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the qualifying conditions are met in that year`
    WHEN JUST met THEN
        IF met
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company qualifies as a micro-entity in relation to its first financial year if the qualifying conditions are met in that year"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text)

-- src:4913 | (3) In relation to a subsequent financial year, where on its balance sheet date a company meets or ceases to meet the qualifying conditions, that affects its qualification as a micro-entity only if it occurs in two consecutive financial years.
@ref s 384A(3) A change affects micro-entity qualification only if it occurs in two consecutive financial years (src:4913)
GIVEN `the qualifying conditions are met in this year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the qualifying conditions were met in the previous year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company qualified as a micro-entity in the previous year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 384A(3) the change in whether the qualifying conditions are met affects the company's qualification as a micro-entity` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that affects its qualification as a micro-entity only if it occurs in two consecutive financial years"
    `s 382(2) the change in whether the qualifying conditions are met affects the company's qualification` `the qualifying conditions are met in this year` `the qualifying conditions were met in the previous year` `the company qualified as a micro-entity in the previous year`

-- src:4912 | (2) Subject to subsection (3), a company qualifies as a micro-entity in relation to a subsequent financial year if the qualifying conditions are met in that year.
@ref s 384A(2) Qualifying as a micro-entity in a subsequent financial year (src:4912)
GIVEN `the qualifying conditions are met in this year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the qualifying conditions were met in the previous year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company qualified as a micro-entity in the previous year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 384A(2) the company qualifies as a micro-entity in a subsequent financial year` MEANS
    `s 382(1A) the company qualifies as small in a subsequent financial year` `the qualifying conditions are met in this year` `the qualifying conditions were met in the previous year` `the company qualified as a micro-entity in the previous year`

-- src:4924 | (8) In the case of a company which is a parent company, the company qualifies as a micro-entity in relation to a financial year only if—
-- src:4925 | (a) the company qualifies as a micro-entity in relation to that year, as determined by subsections (1) to (7), and
-- src:4926 | (b) the group headed by the company qualifies as a small group, as determined by section 383(2) to (7).
@ref s 384A(8) A parent company qualifies as a micro-entity only if its group qualifies as a small group (src:4924-4926)
GIVEN `the company qualifies as a micro-entity in relation to that year, as determined by subsections (1) to (7)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the group headed by the company qualifies as a small group, as determined by section 383(2) to (7)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 384A(8) the parent company qualifies as a micro-entity` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company qualifies as a micro-entity in relation to a financial year only if"
    `s 362 helper both answers` `the company qualifies as a micro-entity in relation to that year, as determined by subsections (1) to (7)` `the group headed by the company qualifies as a small group, as determined by section 383(2) to (7)`

-- ---- s 384B: companies excluded from being treated as micro-entities --------------------------------------------------

-- src:4928 | (1) The micro-entity provisions do not apply in relation to a company’s accounts for a particular financial year if the company ... at any time within that year—
-- src:4929 | (a) was a company excluded from the small companies regime by virtue of section 384,
-- src:4930 | (b) would have been an investment undertaking as defined in Article 2(14) of Directive 2013/34/ EU of 26 June 2013 on the annual financial statements etc. of certain types of undertakings were the United Kingdom a member State,
-- src:4931 | (c) would have been a financial holding undertaking as defined in Article 2(15) of that Directive were the United Kingdom a member State,
-- src:4932 | (d) a credit institution within the meaning given by Article 4(1)(1) of Regulation (EU) No. 575/2013 of the European Parliament and of the Council, which is a CRR firm within the meaning of Article 4(1)(2A) of that Regulation,
-- src:4933 | (e) would have been an insurance undertaking as defined in Article 2(1) of Council Directive 91/674/EEC of 19 December 1991 on the annual accounts of insurance undertakings were the United Kingdom a member State, or
-- src:4934 | (f) was a charity.
@ref s 384B(1) Companies excluded from being treated as micro-entities (src:4928-4934)
GIVEN `s 384 the company was at any time within the year excluded from the small companies regime` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `would have been an investment undertaking as defined in Article 2(14) of Directive 2013/34/EU were the United Kingdom a member State` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `would have been a financial holding undertaking as defined in Article 2(15) of that Directive were the United Kingdom a member State` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `was a credit institution within the meaning given by Article 4(1)(1) of Regulation (EU) No. 575/2013 which is a CRR firm within the meaning of Article 4(1)(2A) of that Regulation` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `would have been an insurance undertaking as defined in Article 2(1) of Council Directive 91/674/EEC were the United Kingdom a member State` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `was a charity` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 384B(1) the micro-entity provisions do not apply to the company's accounts` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The micro-entity provisions do not apply in relation to a company’s accounts for a particular financial year if the company"
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) where a borrowed answer is not known and no other limb decides
    `s 362 helper some answer`
        (LIST `s 384 the company was at any time within the year excluded from the small companies regime`,
              `would have been an investment undertaking as defined in Article 2(14) of Directive 2013/34/EU were the United Kingdom a member State`,
              `would have been a financial holding undertaking as defined in Article 2(15) of that Directive were the United Kingdom a member State`,
              `was a credit institution within the meaning given by Article 4(1)(1) of Regulation (EU) No. 575/2013 which is a CRR firm within the meaning of Article 4(1)(2A) of that Regulation`,
              `would have been an insurance undertaking as defined in Article 2(1) of Council Directive 91/674/EEC were the United Kingdom a member State`,
              `was a charity`)

-- src:4935 | (2) The micro-entity provisions also do not apply in relation to a company’s accounts for a financial year if —
-- src:4936 | (a) the company is a parent company which prepares group accounts for that year as permitted by section 399(4), or
-- src:4937 | (b) the company is not a parent company but its accounts are included in consolidated group accounts for that year.
@ref s 384B(2) The micro-entity provisions also do not apply in two further cases (src:4935-4937)
GIVEN `s 1173(1) the company is a parent company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company prepares group accounts for that year as permitted by section 399(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company's accounts are included in consolidated group accounts for that year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 384B(2) the micro-entity provisions also do not apply to the company's accounts` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The micro-entity provisions also do not apply in relation to a company’s accounts for a financial year if"
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) where the parent-company answer is not known and no limb decides
    `s 362 helper either answer`
        (`s 362 helper both answers` `s 1173(1) the company is a parent company` (JUST `the company prepares group accounts for that year as permitted by section 399(4)`))
        (`s 362 helper both answers` (`s 362 helper the opposite answer` `s 1173(1) the company is a parent company`) (JUST `the company's accounts are included in consolidated group accounts for that year`))

-- ---- s 385: quoted and unquoted companies ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4941 | (2) A “quoted company” means a company whose equity share capital—
-- src:4942 | (a) has been included in the official list in accordance with the provisions of Part 6 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (c. 8), or
-- src:4943 | (b) is officially listed in an EEA State, or
-- src:4944 | (c) is admitted to dealing on either the New York Stock Exchange or the exchange known as Nasdaq.
-- src:4945 | In paragraph (a) “the official list” has the meaning given by section 103(1) of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000.
@ref s 385(2) "quoted company" (src:4941-4945)
-- "officially listed in an EEA State": the EEA State and the official list are borrowed terms (section 1170, the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000).
GIVEN `its equity share capital has been included in the official list in accordance with the provisions of Part 6 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its equity share capital is officially listed in an EEA State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its equity share capital is admitted to dealing on either the New York Stock Exchange or the exchange known as Nasdaq` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 385(2) the company is a quoted company` MEANS
    IF `its equity share capital has been included in the official list in accordance with the provisions of Part 6 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000` OR `its equity share capital is officially listed in an EEA State` OR `its equity share capital is admitted to dealing on either the New York Stock Exchange or the exchange known as Nasdaq`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A “quoted company” means a company whose equity share capital"

-- src:4940 | (1) For the purposes of this Part a company is a quoted company in relation to a financial year if it is a quoted company immediately before the end of the accounting reference period by reference to which that financial year was determined.
@ref s 385(1) Quoted in relation to a financial year (src:4940)
GIVEN `the company is a quoted company immediately before the end of the accounting reference period by reference to which that financial year was determined` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 385(1) the company is a quoted company in relation to the financial year` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the company is a quoted company immediately before the end of the accounting reference period by reference to which that financial year was determined`
    WHEN JUST quoted THEN
        IF quoted
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a company is a quoted company in relation to a financial year if it is a quoted company immediately before the end of the accounting reference period"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text)

-- src:4946 | (3) An “unquoted company” means a company that is not a quoted company.
@ref s 385(3) "unquoted company" (src:4946)
GIVEN `s 385(2) the company is a quoted company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 385(3) the company is an unquoted company` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An “unquoted company” means a company that is not a quoted company"
    `s 362 helper the opposite answer` `s 385(2) the company is a quoted company`

-- s 385(4), (5) and (6) (the Secretary of State's power to amend or replace subsections (1) and (2) by regulations, and the procedure for them):
-- inert, reason 2 (regulation-making powers and parliamentary procedure).
